-### [S3IM (Stochastic Structural SIMilarity)](10895-s3im-stochastic-structural-similarity.md)
-S3IM is a nonlocal multiplex loss function for neural fields that captures structural similarity by processing multiple data points (pixels/rays) as a whole set, rather than individually. It addresses the limitation of point-wise losses (like MSE) which fail to utilize the collective supervision of distant pixels. Unlike conventional MSE, S3IM cannot be expressed as the sum of any other loss computed over individual pixels from the batch.
+### [S3IM](10894-s3im.md)
+S3IM (Stochastic Structural SIMilarity) is a multiplex loss function for neural fields that captures non-local structural similarity by processing multiple data points (pixels/rays) as a whole set, rather than individually. It addresses the limitation of point-wise losses (like MSE) which fail to use collective supervision of distant pixels. Unlike conventional MSE loss which is computed pixel-wisely, S3IM cannot be expressed as the sum of any other loss computed over individual pixels from the batch. It diverges from conventional point-to-point loss functions by analyzing various data points collectively to obtain non-local structural details.
 
